WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.825
Every Florida captain eventually meets a day that turned out worse than the forecast.

2
00:00:06.075 --> 00:00:08.525
This lesson is about that day.

3
00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:12.350
The best heavy-weather tactic is not to be out in it.

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.725
Check the forecast, and when in doubt, don’t go.

5
00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:19.300
No fish is worth it, and neither is a refund.

6
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.850
If the weather catches you anyway, life jackets go on everyone.

7
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.300
Before it’s rough, not during.

8
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.100
Secure the loose gear, and close the hatches and doors.

9
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.950
Slow down.

10
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.400
Pounding into head seas at speed hurts people and breaks boats.

11
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.500
So how do you take them?

12
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.950
At a slight angle off the bow, at a speed that lets her ride up and over each wave.

13
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.475
And keep your passengers seated, low, and near the middle of the boat.

14
00:00:49.725 --> 00:00:52.000
That’s where the motion is least.
